      zoo:text "14 has many a trace of the hoer and the shepherd. Further, while" .

<http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/VARRO/de_re_rustica/e/2/11/text/19>
      a       zoo:Paragraph ;
      zoo:identifier 19 ;
      zoo:isPartOf <http://ns.inria.fr/zoomathia/VARRO/de_re_rustica/e/2/11> ;
      zoo:text "At the same time a freedman of Vitulus, on his way to the city from the park, turned aside to us and said: 'I was sent to you, and was on my way to your house to ask you not to make the holiday shorter but to come early.' And so Scrofa and I set out to Vitulus's place, and the others," .

